sex videos; they get there and they're like,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.940
"Where's the giraffe sex? There's no giraffe
sex! It's just a guy; he's talking. He's not

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.150
very funny; he's got funny hair. I hate this
guy! Click!"

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.010
But then again, Nerdfighteria does a lot of
things other than watch videos like create

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.780
profiles on the Ning, and post in Your Pants,
and post YouTube comments... so let's just

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.070
take a wild guess and say that it averages
out to 3 minutes and 30 seconds, because that's

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.039
a good number for calculation and I'm pretty
bad at math, so I need help.

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:10.710
Okay, so 122 million times 3.5 is... really?
427 million minutes?

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.009
Now, Hank, because I've seen the musical "Rent,"
I know there are 525,600 minutes in a year,

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:20.840
which means that Nerdfighteria is more than
812 years old!

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.189
By the way, Hank, speaking of the amazing
things Nerdfighteria can do because it's 812

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:26.799
years old: Did you know that there are nerdfighters
in Your Pants currently trying to figure out

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:30.780
the mystery of Gussie Manlove, Walter Manlove's
wife? Link in the dooblydoo.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:36.471
So, Hank, we're talking about a total of about
7,116,667 hours. It takes an average of 120

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:39.890
watts per hour for computers to browse the
Internet, so you multiply that big number

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:46.950
times 120, and you get... 854 million, zero
thousand, forty watts. Did I say that number

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.840
right? God, I'm bad at math.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.020
Which is 854,000.04 kilowatts, but I'm going
to eliminate that "zero-four," Hank, because

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.289
it makes the math hard.

00:01:56.289 --> 00:02:00.890
On average, in the US, it takes about 1.35
pounds of carbon to create a kilowatt of energy,

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:09.500
ergo... Nerdfighteria is responsible for 1,152,900
pounds of carbon, which means, Hank, that

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:15.580
Nerdfighteria, in four years, has created
more carbon emissions than the average Swede

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.700
